{"schema":2,"commit":"bf6fdf7ffd88c2423ce9deb9332c06bd3bf51212","branch":"main","base_sha":"9302d1af113042977f60760663d85516a392b2ea","message":"fix: stop leaking a PTY bridge and a shell per pane on every exit\n\npty_bridge.py read the parent's pipe closing as \"drop that fd from the watch\nlist\" and carried on relaying, so a panea that died any way other than a clean\nWebSocket close left every one of its bridges running, each holding a pty\nmaster open and with it a live zsh. The processes were reparented to launchd\nand never reaped: this machine had 174 bridges up, 169 orphaned, the oldest\ntwo days old, ~490 MB across the bridges and their shells. One of them was\nstill running out of a Cellar path for a version that had already been\nuninstalled.\n\nThe bridge now exits when either pipe to its parent closes, and shuts the\nshell down for real -- close the master, SIGHUP, wait, then SIGKILL -- instead\nof relying on the master fd closing to hang it up. The SIGTERM handler goes\nthrough the same path, so Pane.kill() now reaches the shell too.\n\nserver/shutdown.js runs registered teardowns on SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP and\nprocess exit. connection.js registers its pane map there, so signals take the\npanes down instead of only a WebSocket close doing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018t9iga7qxv4tGRzZDQdBMM","coding_time_nanos":169110183000,"totals":{"added_lines":206,"ai_added_lines":204,"human_added_lines":2,"deleted_lines":11,"ai_deleted_lines":10,"human_deleted_lines":1,"files":6,"tokens":{"input":22,"output":9153,"cache_read":1428276,"cache_write":15534},"models":{"claude-opus-5":204}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":204,"deleted_lines":10,"suggested_lines":206,"accepted_lines":204,"tokens":{"input":22,"output":9153,"cache_read":1428276,"cache_write":15534}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":214,"completion":0,"human":3},"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_l